  "description": "issue #674 (SP2): `tell` is a command that changes the addressed set until changed again. After `tell [ :a :b ]`, a second `tell :a` narrows the addressed set to just turtle 1, so the following `forward 50` emits exactly one `move`+`draw-segment` pair, stamped `turtle_id` 1 — turtle 2 does not move. Every change of the addressed set — here from `tell` — also emits the addressing `primitive` event carrying `addressing: { addressed_turtle_ids, current_turtle_id }`, so a consumer can identify the addressed turtle set (issue #766, spec/rendering.md:193); `ask`/`each` emit one again when the previous set is restored, on every exit path.",
